  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-13T23:46:31.168Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Updating world or avatar previews (without updating the worlds or avatars themselves) would be useful, especially if it can be done for Public Worlds and Public Avatars without resetting those Worlds or Avatars to Private again, since sometimes one uploads a world or Avatar, but forgets to update the preview image, or in my case the preview image is a big red \"?\" on a white background, on a public world. I uploaded a preview with the world, and I can see it in the world browser, however, on the world's information, and on the portals to the world, it is as I previously mentioned. This is a public world, and updating the world's preview without having to make it private and resubmit it for public just because of a server hiccup is quite the hassle. I'm sure the same can be said for uploading Avatars.",
